330edc627b9178db0628c3aee0"}]},{"sha":"13d7b546dada1cb2960dec90875b16a42ff7fb84","node_id":"C_kwDOCeQ7u9oAKDEzZDdiNTQ2ZGFkYTFjYjI5NjBkZWM5MDg3NWIxNmE0MmZmN2ZiODQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Lukas Bergdoll","email":"lukas.bergdoll@gmail.com","date":"2024-08-25T17:14:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"Lukas Bergdoll","email":"lukas.bergdoll@gmail.com","date":"2024-08-25T18:47:01Z"},"message":"Add binary-size optimized variants for stable and unstable sort as well as select_nth_unstable\n\n- Stable sort uses a simple merge-sort that re-uses the existing - rather gnarly - merge function.\n- Unstable sort jumps directly to the branchless heapsort fallback.\n- select_nth_unstable jumps directly to the median_of_medians fallback, which is augmented with a\n  custom tiny smallsort and partition impl.\n\nSome code is duplicated but de-duplication would bring it's own problems. For example `swap_if_less`\nis critical for performance, if the sorting networks don't inline it perf drops drastically,\nhowever `#[inline(always)]` is also a poor fit, if the provided comparison function is huge,\nit gives the compiler an out to only instantiate `swap_if_less` once and call it. Another aspect\nthat would suffer when making `swap_if_less` pub, is having to cfg out dozens of functions in\nin smallsort module.","tree":{"sha":"6be63771959b2fecf4326337b802ac09a7ea5566","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anza-xyz/rust/git/trees/6be63771959b2fecf4326337b802ac09a7ea5566"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anza-xyz/rust/git/commits/13d7b546dada1cb2960dec90875b16a42ff7fb84","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anza-xyz/rust/commits/13d7b546dada1cb2960dec90875b16a42ff7fb84","html_url":"https://github.com/anza-xyz/rust/commit/13d7b546dada1cb2960dec90875b16a42ff7fb84","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anza-xyz/rust/commits/13d7b546dada1cb2960dec90875b16a42ff7fb84/comme